drm: h713-afbd: the two windows as plane properties, the plane only places

The bench of 22.09.2026 (dev21, "Q15 bench") measured what the eight window
words do, and the answer is not what 0133b built. They describe a transform
INTO THE CAPTURE RING: words 27..30 are the part of the source the firmware
reads, words 31..34 the part of the ring it writes the result into, and the
firmware skips its scaler altogether when the source window is the whole
frame. With the source window at 480,270 960x540 and the destination left
empty the centre quarter filled the panel at 2x (step c). With the destination
alone at 192,108 1536x864 and a full source window the wall did not move at
all (step a), nor with the source at exactly full or at 1918x1078 (f, g). And
the zoom-out recipe worked: source 0,0 1918x1078, destination 0,0 1536x864,
the plane cropping that region out of the ring (0133c) and placing it at
192,108 - the whole picture at four fifths, centred, with a black band where
it ends (h).

So the plane's CRTC rectangle is the placement on the panel and nothing else,
and it must stop feeding words 31..34. 0133b did that for a reason that
sounded right and measured wrong - "the window is the plane's ordinary
destination rectangle, a private property would only be a second name for the
same four numbers" - and the consequence was a zoom that moved the firmware's
scaler window with nothing to show for it on the wall. The two windows are
their own thing: they are windows in the ring, not on the panel, the plane's
rectangle is a window on the panel, and on a board whose ring is not the panel
(the HY300 Pro's 1280x720) they are not even the same numbers.

They therefore become two plane properties, "src-window" and "dst-window",
each a blob carrying one struct h713_window {x, y, w, h} in PANEL pixels,
converted into the firmware's fixed 30720x17280 space by 0133d's formula and
clamped to it. A blob rather than four range properties per window, because a
window is one object: its four numbers arrive together or not at all, blob id
0 is "absent" without a sentinel value inside the range, and it is two
properties instead of eight that can each be set on their own and leave a
window nobody asked for. That is the smallest encoding that is still correct;
the values are validated in atomic_check against the panel and refused, not
clipped, which is 0133b's own rule kept.

Absent is byte-identical. With both properties at their default the record is
word for word the record this driver published before 0133b existed: words
31..34 become 0, 30720, 0, 17280 by the same arithmetic that a plane covering
its CRTC produced, and words 27..30 keep the ring formula untouched. Proven on
the host by compiling h713_afbd_build_video_info() out of the 181-patch tree
and out of this one and comparing all 36 words over 3 panels x 4 sources x
ring/no-ring x 3 aspect modes (72 cases), with negative controls; the same
harness shows dst-window 192,108 1536x864 reproducing the vendor's own
3072/24576/1728/13824 that 0133b derived from the plane, word for word.

0133e's two module parameters go, and their republish path with them. They
were the bench's handle when nothing else could reach the words; now a client
that sets a window sets it in the same atomic commit that brings the plane up,
which is the path "aspect" has always used. Keeping them would mean two names
for the same eight words - the very thing 0133b was right to warn about - and
it would keep the open question the Q15 review left behind: that republish
reaches into the live plane's state from a sysfs writer and its unbind window
was never closed. Nothing that has to ship should carry that. 0133e's log line
stays, because the eight words are still what an experiment moves.

One more thing the bench decided: the plane does not downscale. With the full
ring as its source and a 1536x864 rectangle as its destination the wall was
smeared, and stayed smeared after the firmware's scaler window had been
written back to 1920x1080 by hand (dev21 "Slot 2b"). 0133b's 128:1 max_scale
assumed the firmware would scale for us on that path; it does not, so the
bound goes back to 1:1 and a request that would need a downscale is refused
instead of shown smeared. can_position stays true - a zoom out is exactly a
1:1 crop placed somewhere on the panel.

What the HY310 sees: nothing, until h713-tv zooms. Without the properties the
plane covers its CRTC and publishes the same 36 words as before, the same
registers are programmed from the same source rectangle, and the only visible
difference is that a plane deliberately made smaller than its CRTC no longer
changes the descriptor - which is what made the old "zoom" do nothing useful.

Follow-up to 0133e (same file, the same eight words); needs nothing else. The
device tree is unchanged - private plane properties need no node.
Sources: umbau/test-20260915/dev21-20260922.md section "Q15 bench" (the table
and the model paragraph), umbau/reviews/Q15.md, umbau/reviews/Q10.md,
AP3c sections 3.4/4.2/5, AP3e sections 2.2/2.5, AP3 section 2.2.

